WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.953
Satchel turns practice questions that a teacher types as plain text into one small file that works without internet,

00:00:07.953 --> 00:00:11.143
on any phone, with a keyboard or a screen reader.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:15.440
This example has five fractions questions, and all five are ready.

00:00:16.443 --> 00:00:20.414
In the preview, the student sees one question at a time,

00:00:20.414 --> 00:00:22.683
with large targets and no timer.

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:25.803
A wrong answer shows the right one, and why.

00:00:26.807 --> 00:00:31.677
Typed answers accept any form the teacher allows, so one half counts as right.

00:00:31.677 --> 00:00:34.487
A hint is there when the student asks for it.

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:40.517
At the end, the student sees what they missed and can practise just those two again.

00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:44.049
Larger text and high contrast are remembered on the device.

00:00:45.052 --> 00:00:49.177
The teacher downloads one HTML file of about twenty-five kilobytes.

00:00:49.177 --> 00:00:52.132
It opens from the downloads folder with no data,

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:56.626
and if scripts are blocked it still lists every question with its answer.

00:00:56.626 --> 00:01:00.012
A paper copy prints with the answers on their own page.
